/v1/","context":{"app_id":5062340,"app_scope":"base","country":"KR","language":"koreana","batch_size":100,"review_scope":"store_summary_filtered","percentage_precision":"source_rounded_integer","review_score_label":"사용자 평가 없음"},"error_code":"no_reviews"}],"events":[{"id":"steam-steam-5062340-1846651706690356","game_id":"steam-5062340","kind":"announcement","title":"Sort My Comics! Demo Available Now for Steam Next Fest!","summary":"If you love comics, organizing things, and the satisfaction of putting everything in its proper place, now's the perfect time to give the game a try!This demo is also your chance to discover a new feature: The Path!Once you've finished sorting all 250 comics in the demo, you'll be able to see the entire route you took throughout your playthrough. This feature will, of course, also be included in the full game!A quick note about save files: To avoid potential compatibility issues, demo saves will","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-19T14:00:31Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706690356","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:24:31Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5062340-1846018067940864","game_id":"steam-5062340","kind":"update","title":"Update 0.5.12","summary":"Controller & Steam DeckAll menus can now be fully navigated with a controller: settings, powers, radio, victory screen, and credits (which can be scrolled using the D-pad or analog stick).The mouse cursor now disappears as soon as you start using a controller.Menu opens the pause menu, while View opens the powers menu. Existing key bindings are automatically migrated, but only if you were still using the default controls.On Steam Deck, the UI now starts at 125% scaling to improve readability on ","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-12T12:59:52Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846018067940864","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:24:31Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5062340-1846018067932647","game_id":"steam-5062340","kind":"update","title":"Update 0.5.9","summary":"NewTwo play modes: all keyboard (E to pick up, R to drop) or mouse (left click to pick up and shelve, right click to drop). Switch at any time from the Pause menu or Options.Powers on keys 1 to 5.Colorblind support: colorblind mode, color correction filter, and cues that no longer rely on color alone.Scalable menus: text and interface size up to 200%, with nothing cut off.Redesigned options: clearer sliders, dropdown lists, a brightness setting, and language selection with flags.New counter at t","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-09T09:09:43Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846018067932647","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:24:31Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5062340-1846018067927723","game_id":"steam-5062340","kind":"announcement","title":"The Demo Is Out Now + 1,000 Wishlists!","summary":"Hi everyone!Today is a pretty special day for Sort My Comics!The free demo is now available on Steam, and almost at the same time, the game has reached 1,000 wishlists.Thank you so much to everyone who has followed the project, shared it, wishlisted it, or simply stopped by to check out this strange little game about sorting thousands of comic books.I work in the video game industry throughout the year as a consultant and game scout, helping teams make their projects stronger, clearer and more e","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-07T22:46:47Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846018067927723","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:24:31Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5062340-1844115010502436","game_id":"steam-5062340","kind":"announcement","title":"The New Trailer Is Here! And the Demo Is Coming October 8!","summary":"Well, here we are! Sort My Comics! has a brand-new trailer! And this time, I can also announce a date for the demo: October 8! Since the Steam page went live, I've been busy working on the game, fixing bugs, improving various systems, and preparing that famous demo. I also wanted to take the time to give you a better look at what you'll actually be doing in the game, with its 2,760 comics to sort, collections to complete, and powers that gradually help you turn this absolute mess into a proper c","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-09-21T20:15:39Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1844115010502436","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:24:31Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5062340-1842212951311898","game_id":"steam-5062340","kind":"announcement","title":"I originally started by making a comic shop simulator","summary":"About a year and a half ago, Sort My Comics! wasn’t a sorting game at all. The original idea was to make a proper comic shop simulator. You’d manage the store, receive comics, put them on shelves, sell them, deal with everything involved in keeping the place running… So, as usual with my personal projects, I had decided to start with something perfectly reasonable and definitely not far too ambitious for someone who was just discovering Unreal Engine. :PBecause yes, at that point, I was basicall","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-09-01T01:24:55Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1842212951311898","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:24:31Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5062340-1842212951300127","game_id":"steam-5062340","kind":"announcement","title":"No artistic talent? Let's figure it out!","summary":"For this game, I had way too many potential 2D visual assets for the covers. If I had the money, I would have loved to let 8 artists imagine their own superheroes and showcase them. But I don't want to underpay anyone, so I'm keeping that idea for later :P So I almost gave up on the comic book idea, and then I stumbled upon a goldmine: the Golden Age of Comics, some of which are in the public domain. On sites like comicbookplus.com, heaps of passionate fans index every comic from that era. Histo","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-08-27T14:00:42Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1842212951300127","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:24:31Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5062340-1841579228676063","game_id":"steam-5062340","kind":"announcement","title":"I made my own cozy sorting game!","summary":"Hello everyone! Allow me to introduce myself: I’m William. Usually, I’m mostly here to help indie devs and game creators release great, polished games with solid marketing, etc. But I’ve always been a failed creator who couldn’t finish his own personal projects. Plus, my ADHD means I can never stick to just one goal. I always have twelve thousand going on at the same time. The result: I never finish anything I start. And making a video game takes time.However, a year ago, after a major burnout d","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-08-24T16:53:19Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1841579228676063","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:24:31Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"}],"analyses":[],"news_status":{"steam-5062340":{"last_